---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'contact@worldradiostations.org';
---
<Base
  title="Content & Copyright Policy — World Radio Stations"
  description="Which streams World Radio Stations plays, where they come from, and how station owners and rights holders can reach us."
>
  <article class="container legal">
    <h1>Content &amp; Copyright Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 6 July 2026</p>

    <p>
      World Radio Stations is a directory and web player for radio stations
      around the world. This page explains where the streams come from, what we
      do and don’t do with them, and how station owners and rights holders can
      contact us.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Where the streams come from</h2>
    <p>
      Station listings come from
      <a href="https://www.radio-browser.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Radio Browser</a>,
      an open community index of internet radio streams. Internet simulcasting is
      how the radio industry reaches listeners: the streams in the index are the
      public stream URLs that stations themselves operate and promote. When you
      press play, the audio comes <strong>directly from the station’s own
      servers</strong> — we do not host, record, re-encode, proxy or rebroadcast
      any audio.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we filter out</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Broken and abandoned streams (checked continuously via the index’s health data).</li>
      <li>Streams not served over a secure (HTTPS) connection.</li>
      <li>Listings reported to us as unauthorized rebroadcasts of another station’s stream.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Trademarks and station materials</h2>
    <p>
      Station names and logos belong to their respective owners and are used
      solely to identify the stations, the way a radio dial or programme guide
      does. Editorial texts — station profiles and blog articles — are our own
      work.
    </p>

    <h2>4. For station owners and rights holders</h2>
    <p>
      If you operate a station and want your stream removed, corrected or added —
      or you believe a listing infringes your rights — email
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the station and the page URL concerned;</li>
      <li>the organisation you represent and your role;</li>
      <li>what you’d like changed (removal, corrected stream URL, updated details).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We act on every such notice promptly — typically within <strong>72
      hours</strong>. Because listings originate in the open Radio Browser index,
      we can also help you correct the source entry so the change sticks
      everywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Mistakes happen</h2>
    <p>
      Stream URLs change hands and community indexes occasionally contain
      errors. If a listing that shouldn’t be here slips through, that is an
      error, not a practice — report it and we will remove it.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
